      "content": "# dbt connection refused — version 1 — 2026-10-20\nSymptoms: connection_refused, connection refused, dbt_orders, dbt_run.\nConfirm: failed task log and selected dbt artifacts identify the failing connection. mcp_readonly success only confirms that separate connection.\nAction: developer checks dbt endpoint, service availability, routing and authentication using explicitly supplied configuration. Do not expose passwords. Correct a port only if endpoint evidence proves it is wrong.\nPrerequisite: establish the actual dbt execution configuration; do not infer an incorrect port from a generic refusal.\nVerification: successful new pipeline execution and passing not_null/unique checks; a successful connection probe alone does not prove recovery.\nExclude: schema and data-quality failures with functioning connectivity. Never claim a specific port from an absent log value.\n",
